WEBVTT

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:19.970
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:19.970
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:19.970
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:05.000
You must be
Siegfried Kircheis.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.110
Captain ?

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:08.240
No, Commander, right ?

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:13.570
I've heard you're Reinhard
von Musel's right-hand man.

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:20.260
Commander, this is my old friend,
Retired Vice Admiral Christopher von Basel.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:21.810
Where's Johanna ?

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.540
She's having a rather
heavy bout of space-sickness.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.110
She's already gone
to our room to rest.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:29.580
She'll come out and
greet you at dinner.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:30.870
Is that so ?

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:33.040
That's okay.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:43.370
I heard you saved my old
friend from a bad situation.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:46.700
I would also like to
express my gratitude.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:51.710
This morning I was
also nearly killed.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.900
Are you trying to insinuate that
yesterday's incident was not accidental...

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:02.110
...but that these occurrences are connected
to one another in a single cause ?

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:04.760
It would only be
natural to think so.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:07.500
That's an interesting theory.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:13.170
Since my friend is being victimized by a
malicious plan, I cannot just disregard this.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.820
I would like to
know the details.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:18.260
I'm not at liberty to
say anything further.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:24.700
The Superintendent has asked for my silence
and I should not make irresponsible inferences.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:29.080
So you say you can only tell me
a small portion of the whole story.

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:32.550
Truly, a very
small portion.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:45.000
By the way, my lord, on which ship
and at what time did you arrive today ?

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.240
At 10:30, I believe.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.400
Why do you want to know ?

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.800
No reason, just asking.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:09.750
Dishonor

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:09.750
Chapter 3

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:23.150
It is indeed strange.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:27.170
Mr. Basel definitely wants to
pretend that he just arrived today.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:32.520
He must have noticed that
I have doubts about it.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:42.020
What matters now is
how he will react to me.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:58.890
It seems like I'm becoming
more and more distrustful.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:37.570
What was that ?

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:07.500
Come on.

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:23.620
Just as I thought, a trap.

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:26.600
Five men is slightly
more than I expected, but...

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:14.630
All right !

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:16.610
I'll bet 500 marks on the red head.

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:18.450
Are you sure ?

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:20.310
He's alone.

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:26.580
Well, he must be damn strong, 
he's got a five to one handicap.

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:28.400
Of course I am.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:31.100
You, bet 500 marks
on the other guys.

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:32.410
Don't decide that for me.

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:47.080
This is for real !

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:49.520
Call the police !

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:53.550
Yeah, this is a real fight !

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:56.000
I'll raise the
bet to 1000 marks !

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:57.790
This is well worth it !

00:08:57.790 --> 00:08:59.620
Hang on, Red !

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:02.410
I'll bet my life on you !

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:11.400
Two down.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:12.400
Why you...!

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:41.200
Shit !

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:45.560
Oh, no !

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:46.450
Shit.

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:47.090
Downstairs !

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:48.370
Get to the ground floor !

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:49.850
Yes, sir !

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:53.760
Are you all right, Commander ?

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:55.170
Yes, somehow.

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:56.810
You saved me.

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:59.120
Thank you for
your timely help.

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:03.590
I just had a report from
the surveillance center.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:07.330
They said the monitors in the flying
ball stadium weren't working.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:12.510
Even if I were dull-witted, I'd be hard-pressed
not to think something might be happening.

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:18.900
But anyway, what a fine job you did,
surviving a five on one fight.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:21.000
If you had been late by
another three minutes...

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.150
...I wouldn't have been alive
to hear your compliments.

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:27.370
Well, it was difficult to judge
when to turn off the switch.

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:28.610
It was as
timely as it gets.

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:33.410
We discovered the escaped
assailant downstairs.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:35.730
We've cornered him in the
terrace by the waterfall, but...

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:36.970
What happened ?

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:39.550
He's taken a hostage.

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:40.250
What ?

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:42.080
We should go there.

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:43.230
Right.

00:10:56.110 --> 00:10:57.070
There he is.

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:01.510
Can't you see this knife ?

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:02.900
Don't do it !

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:04.480
Let me go !

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:06.100
Don't come near me !

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:07.180
Don't come any closer !

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:11.960
It's looking bad.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:22.550
Superintendent, can
I borrow your handgun ?

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:23.300
Eh ?

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:27.300
We're quite a distance away...

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:28.360
I'll give it a try.

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:29.940
But...

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:30.840
Quickly !

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:51.190
A spaceship !

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:53.810
Give me a spaceship !

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:55.040
Or I'll...

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:02.750
Now !

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:09.260
Superintendent, we've
arrested the suspect.

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:10.300
The hostage is safe, too.

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:11.860
Good.

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:14.160
But what shooting
skill you've got.

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:17.090
You aimed at his knife
and didn't shoot to kill.

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:18.000
Thank you.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.170
No, no.

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:21.200
You can keep it.

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:33.700
I suppose shooting skills
can be useful sometimes.

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:35.850
The other four
men are dead...

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:38.470
...but it's a coup that we
have taken one of them alive.

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:40.480
We might be able to get
some information out of him.

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:42.330
He might just
be a hired gun.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:45.090
Retired Vice Admiral Basel...

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:48.600
Right ?

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:58.950
What you said earlier bugged
me, so I looked into it.

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:02.400
There were a couple of things
that piqued our interest.

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:03.950
Such as ?

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:06.590
The first item is
what you already know:

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:12.300
The Basels arrived at Kreuznach III earlier
than scheduled and were staying here.

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:15.170
We could easily find
out these things.

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:18.940
If you had told me, that
would have been better.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:20.770
But I forgive you.

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:24.070
But there is another thing
that concerns me even more.

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:27.080
Of course, I'll gladly provide
you with the information.

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:31.720
About that
chief petty officer...

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:36.810
...he was in the Keyserling Fleet three
years ago, as I've already informed you.

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:42.920
We looked into it further, and found out
that he was part of the supply regiment.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:44.470
Supply regiment ?

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:45.530
Yes.

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:48.040
At the time, he was presumed
to be in a supply ship...

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:52.950
...but the issue here is that the man in
charge of supplies for the Keyserling Fleet...

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:57.570
...was the rear-line primary chief
officer, Rear Admiral Basel.

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:03.100
Even more important is the fact that
just before the Battle of Arlesheim...

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:10.470
...Rear Admiral Basel was investigated by the
Military Police on suspicion of possessing Thyoxin.

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:21.400
Of course, he was acquitted at the
time, but the key to that acquittal...

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:26.950
...was the testimony by his superior
at the time, Vice Admiral Keyserling.

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:33.970
This is what I think:

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:39.950
That the Keyserling Fleet was contaminated by the drug on the fleet level...

00:14:39.950 --> 00:14:46.910
...with Admiral Keyserling and Rear-Line
Chief Officer Basel in charge of it.

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:51.190
Using the infrastructure that they
had established within the military...

00:14:51.190 --> 00:14:54.670
...those two continued to traffic
the drug even after they retired.

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:57.790
But some sort of conflict
arose inside that organization...

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:00.550
...leading to this series of
incidents we've witnessed so far.

00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:01.960
What do you think ?

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:02.930
Have you got any evidence ?

00:15:02.930 --> 00:15:05.950
None, at least so far.

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:10.850
If we can get information out of the assailant
we just arrested, we might have a lead...

00:15:10.850 --> 00:15:17.950
...but as you said, he could just be a hired
gun, so there may not be much hope.

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:22.750
May I have a
window of time ?

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:30.660
Commander ?

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:36.420
Well, thank you for coming.

00:15:36.420 --> 00:15:37.540
Please come in.

00:15:38.090 --> 00:15:39.000
If you'll excuse me.

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:46.980
Would you like some coffee ?

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:48.090
No, thank you.

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:01.800
At the time of the
Battle of Arlesheim...

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:05.740
...you were the Commander of the
Fleet, and Vice Admiral Basel...

00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:08.300
...no, he was a Rear
Admiral back then...

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:12.550
...was a rear-line chief officer
in charge of supply lines.

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:13.660
Is this correct ?

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:24.290
At the time, Rear Admiral Basel was investigated by the Military Police for possession of Thyoxin...

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:27.350
...and was summoned to court.

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:35.240
That suspicion was cleared by your testimony,
Vice Admiral Keyserling, and he was acquitted.

00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:42.040
The loss at Arlesheim took place
about a month afterwards.

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:43.960
What are you
trying to say ?

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:51.400
Wasn't the cause of the defeat of the Imperial
Fleet the acute intoxication of the sailors...

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:56.430
...the result of the vaporization of the
drug that triggered hallucinations ?

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:05.730
You did not testify to that
effect at the court martial.

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:10.750
If you had done it, Vice Admiral Basel would
have been the one to be held responsible.

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:16.800
You saved your romantic
rival by your silence.

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:19.130
Am I correct ?

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:23.120
Why ?

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:27.180
Why did you extend yourself that far
to cover for Vice Admiral Basel ?

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:32.220
That's such a
one-sided sacrifice.

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:36.400
Because of what happened, he was
demoted and discharged from the military...

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:42.310
...while Basel was promoted to Vice Admiral
later, and their positions were reversed.

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:54.720
It's not really a difficult
question to answer.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:18:02.770
The man she chose, whom Johanna
chose, cannot be a criminal.

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:14.510
Johanna chose a man who was worthy of her,
a man of integrity and substance, her equal.

00:18:15.630 --> 00:18:16.580
That's...

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:33.160
Is this his belief ?

00:18:33.740 --> 00:18:35.150
Or his delusion ?

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:38.750
Is it something that can be
refuted with logic and reason ?

00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:56.180
But what about your honor ?

00:18:56.830 --> 00:19:00.060
My honor{reputation} is of
little importance.

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:06.290
Besides, it is a fact that I could not control
my subordinates' confusion and disarray.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:09.600
The court martial did not
hold me responsible unjustly.

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:11.300
Then let me rephrase it.

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:18.330
What's unjust is not that you were punished but that Vice Admiral Basel escaped his share of the blame.

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:22.300
Won't you testify to
right that injustice ?

00:19:22.690 --> 00:19:26.050
No, I can't do that, Commander.

00:19:26.050 --> 00:19:31.650
If I cooperate in exposing his crime, 
people will say that I was crazed by envy...

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:34.620
...and forgot forty years of
friendship because of it.

00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:37.900
But if I may retort...

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:45.000
...you previously accepted the undeserved
infamy of being an "incompetent coward."

00:19:46.900 --> 00:19:50.330
Will you say that you can accept such
dishonor for the woman you love...

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:55.250
...but that you won't do the same for the many
people who suffer from drug intoxication ?

00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:20.920
It seems I forgot to say
something the other day.

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:28.750
Being young also means you don't
hesitate to pursue social justice.

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:33.770
Three years ago, I had 
already lost such youthfulness.

00:20:35.070 --> 00:20:40.120
All I thought about was that I
didn't want to make her unhappy.

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:49.530
But justice or love can sometimes be a
burden to those who are its recipients.

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:53.460
Life is not
elementary arithmetic.

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:57.390
Formulas can't find
solutions for everything.

00:20:57.390 --> 00:21:04.400
If we knew a certain amount of reward would result from a certain amount of devotion...

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:07.690
...life would be so
simple and clear.

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:15.300
Commander, you are right...

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:17.390
...more right than I am.

00:21:17.390 --> 00:21:21.400
If I had publicized the
facts three years ago...

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:27.500
...I could have at least prevented new
Thyoxin addiction cases afterwards.

00:21:28.860 --> 00:21:34.810
I sacrificed those soldiers
for my own sentimentality.

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:41.230
They too must have had people they loved,
things they wanted to pursue or protect.

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:44.630
I was an intractable narcissist.

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:48.450
I brought no one happiness.

00:21:50.790 --> 00:21:55.310
He did not look for compensation
in his devotion toward Mrs. Basel.

00:21:55.310 --> 00:21:58.450
Is it a noble feeling ?

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:04.260
Or is it just egoism ?

00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:12.500
As he witnessed the regretful and
self-reproaching Keyserling...

00:22:12.500 --> 00:22:15.610
...Kircheis was starting
to feel they were alike.

00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:22.950
The relationship of the three bore similarities
to that of Kircheis, Reinhard and Annerose...

00:22:22.950 --> 00:22:26.700
...he wondered where his own
three-way relationship would lead.

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:30.450
But he could not bog himself down
in such introspection for long.

00:22:31.350 --> 00:22:35.470
For the case in front of him
had not yet been resolved.

00:22:36.400 --> 00:22:41.900
To be continued

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:49.050
[ Time to Mourn, Time to Celebrate ]

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:49.050
Ending Theme

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:49.050
Vocals: Ogura Kei

